diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1b7e118..b8ea124 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ Core endpoints:
 
 Customers register in a portal, verify their email, and use the same session and recovery endpoints as staff. Admins can invite verified staff as admins or agents. Invitation links point to the frontend acceptance screen and remain valid for seven days. Invitation previews and acceptance require only the unguessable token; acceptance creates an already-verified user.
 
-Request and ticket lists support `page` and `per_page`; they include pagination metadata and newest account activity first. Comment lists are oldest first. Ticket replies are stored as portal comments and do not send email. Staff may add public comments or private notes and assign tickets to active staff members. Assignment-only activity and private notes do not alter the customer request's activity timestamp.
+Request and ticket lists support `page` and `per_page`; they include pagination metadata and newest account activity first. Customers can filter their requests by `status`. Staff can combine `status`, `assignee_id`, `requester_id`, `priority`, and literal, case-insensitive `q` search across subjects and public comments. Use `assignee_id=unassigned` for tickets without an assignee. Comment lists are oldest first. Ticket replies are stored as portal comments and do not send email. Staff may add public comments or private notes, assign tickets to active staff members, and set their priority to `normal` or `high`. Priority defaults to `normal` and is only exposed on staff ticket responses. Assignment, priority-only, and private-note activity do not alter the customer request's activity timestamp.
 
 Admin people lists can filter with `role` and `suspended`; invitation lists can filter with `status`. People and invitation lists use ascending IDs, as do active staff choices. Suspending a staff member revokes their sessions and clears their ticket assignments. The last active admin cannot be suspended.
 
